Terminalia is a variant of the Terminus font, based on the Terminus
TTF, and extended to support Cyrillic and some other alphabets.

The original Terminus is a bitmap font, but using bitmap fonts on
modern displays, with a large variety of DPIs, sizes, and subpixel
orderings is a pain.

Vectorizing fonts is, unfortunately, also a pain, and extending fonts
to support non-Roman alphabets with a matching style, is also not
easy.

Terminalia should be one of the approaches of doing it. It is a part
of the LOCALFONTS project, which are trying to accomplish the same for
many other popular typefaces:

https://github.com/StefanPeev/Terminalia#localfonts-projects

It does _NOT_ support Chinese.

This packages installs only the "default" OTF version.

There are other versions:

1. web ttf
2. autohinted ttf
3. variable ttf

If anyone knows what the difference is, drop the maintainer a message.
